 "disclosure": "Mercury (P-M) disclosure: production acquisition was stopped at sentinel time point 3 by the original pre-registered drift gate (P9-005). That gate was then shown, from pre-production smoke data and the frozen sentinel composition, to be statistically miscalibrated (estimated false-stop probability 0.37-0.49 under smoke-consistent models). After the stop, it was replaced (P9-006) by a stratified, 1% family-wise rule derived from the same pre-production information only. The first 1,708 responses were retained and are included in every Mercury estimate reported here, and acquisition resumed; P-M passed time point 4 under the amended rule. The amended rule needs a single BOTH-cell sentinel to move about 0.27 to stop, so its sensitivity to drift in that cell is weak; this remains a limitation.",
